# BusyBox inittab.
#
# Format: <tty>:<runlevel>:<action>:<command>. BusyBox ignores the runlevel; an
# empty tty means /dev/console, the board's only terminal.
#
# No getty or login: the console is a UART with no access control, so the shell
# is started directly. The leading '-' makes it a login shell, which reads
# /etc/profile.

::sysinit:/etc/init.d/rcS

# respawn: exiting the shell starts a new one.
::respawn:-/bin/sh

::shutdown:/bin/umount -a -r
::shutdown:/bin/sync
